  "body": "Build the CPython extension against the stable ABI (`Py_LIMITED_API=0x030B0000`) so a single `cp311-abi3` wheel covers Python 3.11 and every later version, instead of one wheel per Python version.\n\nThe supported range does not shrink: `python_requires` stays `>=3.11`, the wheel platform matrix (Linux `auto`/`aarch64`/`ppc64le`/`s390x`, macOS `x86_64`/`universal2`/`arm64`, Windows) is untouched, PyPy keeps its per-version wheels, and free-threaded CPython keeps building against its own ABI.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/reader.c`** — define the `Reader` type with `PyType_FromSpec`/`PyType_Slot` instead of a static `PyTypeObject` (the `PyTypeObject` struct is not part of the limited API), and fetch `tp_free` through `PyType_GetSlot`.\n- **`src/pack.c`** — replace `PyMemoryView_GET_BUFFER` (declared in `cpython/memoryobject.h`) with `PyObject_GetBuffer`.\n- **`src/reader.c`, `src/pack.c`** — include `<string.h>` explicitly; `Python.h` no longer pulls it in under the limited API.\n- **`setup.py`** — define `Py_LIMITED_API` and set `py_limited_api` for CPython only. The `bdist_wheel` option is set here rather than in `setup.cfg` because setuptools rejects `py_limited_api` when `Py_GIL_DISABLED` is set, so it has to be conditional.\n\nNo CI change is needed: cibuildwheel finds the already-built abi3 wheel (`find_compatible_wheel`) and skips the redundant per-version builds, and it runs `abi3audit` on abi3 wheels automatically.\n\n## Behaviour change\n\nA **non-contiguous** memoryview such as `memoryview(b\"abcdef\")[::2]` used to silently pack the wrong bytes (`b\"abc\"` instead of `b\"ace\"`), because the old code read `Py_buffer.buf`/`len` straight off the memoryview. It now raises `BufferError`. Contiguous memoryviews are unaffected.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `abi3audit` on the built wheel: **0 ABI violations, 0 version mismatches**.\n- Existing test suite: **105 passed**, including the GC and subclassing tests.\n- The same wheel runs on CPython **3.11, 3.12, 3.14 and 3.15**.\n- Compiles under the limited API with `-Werror` against the 3.11 / 3.12 / 3.14 / 3.15 headers.\n- `python setup.py bdist_wheel` still produces `libvalkey-4.2.0-cp314-cp314t-*` on free-threaded 3.14t.\n- A/B comparison of the module surface before and after: the only difference is `Reader.__flags__` gaining `Py_TPFLAGS_HEAPTYPE`.\n- Microbenchmarks (`feed`+`gets`, `pack_command`, construction) differ by ~2–5%. A control build that changes only the type definition shows the same shift on `pack_command`, which never touches `Reader`, so most of that is binary layout noise in a tight loop.\n",
